HST Office: a second office that only asks for a new document of a module does not wait for it.

`soffice --writer|--calc|--impress` started while HST Office runs hands its request to the running
office over the single-instance pipe (D-Bus on Linux) and used to wait until the request had been
processed. The macOS launchers HST Writer, HST Sheets and HST Slides do exactly this when the office
is running (scripts/macos/hst-app-launcher.m). A new presentation first shows Impress's modal
template dialog ("Lựa chọn mẫu"), so the second soffice, a second HST Office in the Dock, stayed
until the user closed that dialog, its launcher waited 30 s, and the pipe thread accepted no other
request meanwhile (launcher probe run 42938224519, three-apps.png and processes.log).

A request that only creates a new document of a module (no file, print or conversion) is answered
as soon as it is queued; the document is created exactly as before. Requests with files still wait.

License: modified upstream files keep their license (MPL-2.0).
---
--- a/desktop/source/app/officeipcthread.cxx
+++ b/desktop/source/app/officeipcthread.cxx
@@ -901,6 +901,7 @@
     }
 
     bool bDocRequestSent = false;
+    bool bModuleStartOnly = false;
 
     OUString aUnknown( aCmdLineArgs->GetUnknown() );
     if (aUnknown.isEmpty() && !aCmdLineArgs->IsHelp() && !aCmdLineArgs->IsVersion())
@@ -979,6 +980,10 @@
             // the first process, see OpenClients() (call to OpenDefault()) in app.cxx
             if ( aCmdLineArgs->HasModuleParam() && !bDocRequestSent )
             {
+                // HST Office: a new document of a module needs no answer. The second process
+                // (the HST Writer/Sheets/Slides launchers' hand-over) must not wait while the
+                // new document shows a modal dialog, e.g. Impress's template selection.
+                bModuleStartOnly = true;
                 SvtModuleOptions aOpt;
                 SvtModuleOptions::EFactory eFactory = SvtModuleOptions::EFactory::WRITER;
                 if ( aCmdLineArgs->IsWriter() )
@@ -1080,7 +1085,7 @@
             ImplPostForeignAppEvent( pAppEvent );
         }
     }
-    *waitProcessed = bDocRequestSent;
+    *waitProcessed = bDocRequestSent && !bModuleStartOnly;
     return true;
 }
 
